   -- THE COMPONENTS voxelbit.exe REDISTRIBUTES --------------------------------
   The packaged build is not source. It carries third-party BINARIES, and each
   of them travels under its own licence, which this one does not override:

     NVIDIA         DLSS and DLSS Ray Reconstruction, Streamline (frame
                    generation and Reflex), NGX, PhysX 5, NRD, the RTXGI
                    libraries, NVAPI and the CUDA runtime -- under the NVIDIA
                    licences accepted when those SDKs were obtained.
     Falcor         NVIDIA's rendering framework, BSD-3-Clause. Its notice is
                    at v1/external/falcor/LICENSE.md in this repository and
                    travels with the framework it covers.
     Slang          the shader compiler and its runtime, Apache-2.0.
     CPython        the embedded interpreter Falcor initialises at startup,
                    under the PSF licence. Its own package notices are shipped
                    beside it in app/pythondist/PACKAGE-LICENSES.
     Others         FreeImage, OpenEXR/Imath, assimp, OpenVDB and the D3D12
                    Agility SDK, each under its own terms.

   This section is a statement of what is in the file, not a grant. Section 3
   still applies to voxelbit itself: being handed a copy of the game does not
   licence you to redistribute it.

